From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hotty Agent <hotty@neuroplast.io>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 23:03:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vello_cpu: a clip layer nothing is drawn in is not pushed

`push_clip_layer` now keeps the layer back and gives it to the dispatcher
just before the first draw inside it; a clip layer popped before any draw
is dropped. Such a layer changes no pixel, and pushing it costs the clip
path's strips and the layer's bookkeeping. A draw of an empty path (a
space's glyph) does not count as a draw. A held layer also goes to the
dispatcher before any other layer, and before a clip path is pushed or
popped, so its clip is cut by the same clip paths as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/render.rs | 192 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 189 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

